      "dcterms:title": "THE COMPLEX VOLUME OF SL(n, C)-REPRESENTATIONS OF 3-MANIFOLDS",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "GAROUFALIDIS, STAVROS",
        "THURSTON, DYLAN P.",
        "ZICKERT, CHRISTIAN K."
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20180426",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1111.2828",
      "dcterms:abstract": "For a compact 3-manifold M with arbitrary (possibly empty) boundary, we give a parametrization of the set of conjugacy classes of boundary-unipotent representations of π1(M) into SL(n, C). Our parametrization uses Ptolemy coordinates, which are inspired by coordinates on higher Teichmüller spaces due to Fock and Goncharov. We show that a boundary-unipotent representation determines an element in Neumann’s extended Bloch group bB(C), and use this to obtain an eﬃcient formula for the Cheeger-Chern-Simons invariant, and in particular for the vol- ume. Computations for the census manifolds show that boundary-unipotent representations are abundant, and numerical comparisons with census volumes, suggest that the volume of a represen- tation is an integral linear combination of volumes of hyperbolic 3-manifolds. This is in agreement with a conjecture of Walter Neumann, stating that the Bloch group is generated by hyperbolic manifolds.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-1111.2828v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-1111.2828v2"
    }
  ]
}
